! Example initial-conditions namelist for INITIAL_CONDITIONS::READ_IC_NAMELIST
! (src/core/initial_conditions.f90). Wired in 2026-09-27 as an optional,
! 8th CLI argument to app/mhdvsh_hall_crust_profile.f90 (ic_namelist_path
! -- see that driver's own header); absent, the driver falls back to its
! original hardcoded seed unchanged. See ROADMAP.md programming task 4
! for the module's overall status.
!
! &IC_SELECT names the list of ACTIVE tags (composable by design,
! 2026-08-29: every active tag's contribution accumulates into the same
! Phi/Psi, so e.g. a future force-free base plus a Bessel-Riccati
! perturbation could both be listed here at once). READ_IC_NAMELIST then
! reads whichever model-specific group(s) those tags name. Only
! 'bessel_riccati' exists so far, so this example lists just the one.
&IC_SELECT
  N_TAGS = 1
  TAGS   = 'bessel_riccati'
/

! Each mode contributes f_n(x) = A*x*j_n(x) + B*x*y_n(x), x = X_SCALE*r,
! to either PHI or PSI at spherical-harmonic degree/order (L,M). Modes
! sharing the same (FIELD,L,M) accumulate (superpose), so a single
! (l,m) can carry a multi-n radial spectrum by repeating it across
! several array entries. j_n/y_n are evaluated by SPHERICAL_BESSEL --
! stable to n=20 (src/core/spherical_bessel.f90).
!
! MODE_X_SCALE below is NOT an arbitrary 1.0 -- it's tuned (2026-09-27)
! so that x*j_0(x)=sin(x) vanishes almost exactly at both this driver's
! own live TOV-derived crust boundaries, R_min=10.3029 km and
! R_max=11.5621 km (X_SCALE=8*pi/R_min puts a zero of sin(x) exactly at
! R_min and within ~7% of a zero at R_max, the closest integer-multiple-
! of-pi match for this R_max/R_min ratio). This matters empirically, not
! just cosmetically: a first attempt at this example used a plain
! X_SCALE=1 (reducing to the naive Phi(l=1,m=0,r)=sin(r), which is O(1)
! and non-vanishing at both boundaries) and reliably triggered
! mhdvsh_hall_crust_profile's own blow-up detector within ~1-2 outer
! steps, REGARDLESS of cfl_safety (tested down to 50x smaller dt_hall)
! or overall mode amplitude (tested down to 1000x smaller A) -- i.e. a
! genuine boundary-localized Hall instability, not an ordinary CFL/
! discretization artifact, tied to the single outermost grid node's
! already-documented extreme Rmag (~126 even after this driver's own
! truncation; see that driver's header). Forcing the mode to vanish at
! the boundaries (this file) instead of just scaling its amplitude
! removes the trigger; verified stable (energy decreasing, no blowup)
! over a 2000-step / ~1000yr-scale run of mhdvsh_hall_crust_profile.
! This is still just a hand-picked, approximately-boundary-consistent
! mode, NOT the true force-free/BC-exact eigenmode (that needs the
! still-deferred transcendental-eigenvalue root-finder, ROADMAP.md
! programming task 4) -- it's a stable worked example, not a physical
! claim.
&BESSEL_RICCATI_MODES
  N_MODES      = 1
  MODE_FIELD   = 'phi'
  MODE_L       = 1
  MODE_M       = 0
  MODE_N       = 0
  MODE_X_SCALE = 2.4393851467759897
  MODE_A       = 1.0
  MODE_B       = 0.0
/
